## 3. Primary keys and AUTOINCREMENT

Setup:

```sql
CREATE TABLE t_int_pk (id int PRIMARY KEY, name text);
CREATE TABLE t_integer_pk (id integer PRIMARY KEY, name text);
CREATE TABLE t_autoinc (id integer PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name text);
CREATE TABLE t_text_pk (id text PRIMARY KEY, name text);
CREATE TABLE t_composite (a int, b text, PRIMARY KEY (a, b));
```

Command: `/tmp/atlas_orig schema inspect -u "sqlite://pk.db"` — exit `0`, stderr empty. Stdout:

```hcl
table "t_int_pk" {
  schema = schema.main
  column "id" {
    null = true
    type = int
  }
  column "name" {
    null = true
    type = text
  }
  primary_key {
    columns = [column.id]
  }
}
table "t_integer_pk" {
  schema = schema.main
  column "id" {
    null = true
    type = integer
  }
  column "name" {
    null = true
    type = text
  }
  primary_key {
    columns = [column.id]
  }
}
table "t_autoinc" {
  schema = schema.main
  column "id" {
    null           = true
    type           = integer
    auto_increment = true
  }
  column "name" {
    null = true
    type = text
  }
  primary_key {
    columns = [column.id]
  }
}
table "t_text_pk" {
  schema = schema.main
  column "id" {
    null = true
    type = text
  }
  column "name" {
    null = true
    type = text
  }
  primary_key {
    columns = [column.id]
  }
}
table "t_composite" {
  schema = schema.main
  column "a" {
    null = true
    type = int
  }
  column "b" {
    null = true
    type = text
  }
  primary_key {
    columns = [column.a, column.b]
  }
}
schema "main" {
}
```

Key observations:

- `int PRIMARY KEY` vs `integer PRIMARY KEY`: both render as a `primary_key { columns = ... }`
  block; the column keeps its own declared type (`int` vs `integer`). Neither renders
  `null = false` for the PK column — both show `null = true`.
- `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT` adds `auto_increment = true` as a third attribute, and the
  block's `=` signs are **aligned to the longest attribute name** (`null           = true` etc.).
  This alignment is hclwrite-style formatting: consecutive attributes in one block are padded so
  their `=` line up.
- Composite PK: single `primary_key` block, `columns = [column.a, column.b]` (one space after the
  comma, no space before `]`... i.e. exactly `[column.a, column.b]`).
- Tables are emitted in **creation order** (sqlite_master rowid order), not alphabetical.

