## 6. Table-level constraints: FKs and CHECKs

Setup:

```sql
CREATE TABLE parent (id integer PRIMARY KEY, code text UNIQUE);
CREATE TABLE child (
  id integer PRIMARY KEY,
  parent_id int REFERENCES parent(id) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE SET NULL,
  code text,
  age int CHECK (age >= 0),
  FOREIGN KEY (code) REFERENCES parent(code) ON DELETE RESTRICT,
  CONSTRAINT chk_age CHECK (age < 150)
);
```

Command: `/tmp/atlas_orig schema inspect -u "sqlite://constraints.db"` — exit `0`, stderr empty.
Stdout:

```hcl
table "parent" {
  schema = schema.main
  column "id" {
    null = true
    type = integer
  }
  column "code" {
    null = true
    type = text
  }
  primary_key {
    columns = [column.id]
  }
  index "sqlite_autoindex_parent_1" {
    unique  = true
    columns = [column.code]
  }
}
table "child" {
  schema = schema.main
  column "id" {
    null = true
    type = integer
  }
  column "parent_id" {
    null = true
    type = int
  }
  column "code" {
    null = true
    type = text
  }
  column "age" {
    null = true
    type = int
  }
  primary_key {
    columns = [column.id]
  }
  foreign_key "0" {
    columns     = [column.code]
    ref_columns = [table.parent.column.code]
    on_update   = NO_ACTION
    on_delete   = RESTRICT
  }
  foreign_key "1" {
    columns     = [column.parent_id]
    ref_columns = [table.parent.column.id]
    on_update   = SET_NULL
    on_delete   = CASCADE
  }
  check {
    expr = "(age >= 0)"
  }
  check "chk_age" {
    expr = "(age < 150)"
  }
}
schema "main" {
}
```

Rules:

- Inline FKs (`REFERENCES ...`) and table-level FKs both become `foreign_key` blocks named by
  their **ordinal position as a decimal string** (`"0"`, `"1"`), sorted by name (so `"0"` comes
  first even though it was declared second). FK inspection works without `_fk=1` in the URL.
- `on_update`/`on_delete` render unquoted with spaces as `_`: `NO_ACTION`, `RESTRICT`,
  `SET_NULL`, `CASCADE`. Missing actions render `NO_ACTION`. Attribute order: `columns`,
  `ref_columns`, `on_update`, `on_delete` — all aligned.
- `ref_columns` uses cross-table references: `[table.parent.column.code]`.
- Unnamed CHECK constraints render as a `check` block **without a label**; named ones
  (`CONSTRAINT chk_age CHECK ...`) as `check "chk_age"`. `expr` keeps original parentheses.
- Block order inside a table: `column`s (declaration order), `primary_key`, `foreign_key`s,
  `check`s. Indexes appear after `primary_key` when present (see `parent`: pk then index).

