## 11. General formatting notes (apply to all HCL inspect output)

- Output ends with a single trailing newline; no blank line between the last table block and
  `schema "main" { }` block... precisely: blocks are separated by exactly one newline (no blank
  lines anywhere in inspect HCL output).
- Indentation: 2 spaces per level.
- Every table block starts with `schema = schema.main`; output ends with
  `schema "main" {\n}\n`.
- Attribute `=` alignment: within a block, consecutive attributes are padded so all `=` signs
  align with the longest attribute name (e.g. `null           = true` /
  `type           = integer` / `auto_increment = true`).
- Column block attribute order: `null`, `type`, then optional `default`, then optional `as {}`.
- Table block member order: `column`s in declaration order, then `primary_key`, `index`es,
  `foreign_key`s, `check`s, then the `strict` attribute last.
- Tables emitted in creation (sqlite_master) order.
- No color/TTY-dependent formatting in `schema inspect` output; piped and pseudo-TTY output are
  identical modulo the pty's `\n`→`\r\n` translation.
